tined return traffic via node1. After node2's firewall was scoped to expose 8080 only on the eth1 (private) zone, node3 direct access to node2's public/default-network IP was confirmed refused (EXIT=7 curl error) while access via the tunnel path to node2's private IP succeeded, both before and after all three nodes were restarted.\",\"evidence_ids\":[\"cmd-a9bfe48c459a485e\",\"cmd-72adc360d73444db\",\"cmd-88dfe5b7f7df4a66\",\"cmd-2feca923ad4645e6\",\"cmd-0168da1a63eb453e\",\"cmd-cb7d372491fb4fbb\",\"cmd-6c3f6198da294337\",\"cmd-72d98a7986d146a8\",\"cmd-5fa0e9afd090433b\",\"cmd-98008adfa6574d36\"]},{\"id\":\"R5\",\"requirement\":\"Provider-wide node-restart evidence protocol executed on every managed node (independent of task contract)\",\"status\":\"satisfied\",\"summary\":\"All three nodes show a complete restart cycle: pre-restart healthy baseline and boot_id, an acknowledged restart command, a distinct post-restart boot_id, and recovered application/tunnel/network state. node1: ebd78841...→60449fa0..., eth1/wg0/peer config intact post-reboot. node2: 738d0aac...→a919a07f..., webapp.service active and route/eth1 intact (after a pre-reboot corrective restart of a failed webapp unit). node3: 3dba43a5...→915d5f4c..., wg-quick@wg0 active with automatic re-handshake. All boot-id transitions are independently corroborated by the fixed before/after-executor lifecycle snapshots, and full end-to-end app reachability through the tunnel was re-verified after all three restarts completed.\",\"evidence_ids\":[\"cmd-224b4fa72db242d4\",\"cmd-ba3c9e5e8ddb4ed0\",\"cmd-1284af0712aa4f84\",\"cmd-8c1328ee34214b0e\",\"cmd-a7c61595213b4a77\",\"cmd-c4e2b0c49bdf4c6b\",\"cmd-c77a08c3bb7a4cbc\",\"cmd-002d4e0285c34f93\",\"cmd-4a3e2e4c61894c73\",\"cmd-98f3ce4cd3af4555\",\"cmd-2ed65e8bb26f4e8b\",\"cmd-ba4c187ade8d47c5\",\"cmd-5fa0e9afd090433b\",\"cmd-98008adfa6574d36\",\"global:before_prepare:node1:boot-identity\",\"global:after_executor:node1:boot-identity\",\"global:before_prepare:node2:boot-